*rsconnect/
copy_pdf_to_google_drive.R

# Comment out (and thus do not ignore these files) only when version bumping
# the release branch
docs/*
bib/packages.bib

# Instructor-only solutions HTML (rendered separately from the book; never deployed)
/instructor-solutions/_site/
/instructor-solutions/.quarto/
/instructor-solutions/coverage-map.html
/instructor-solutions/concept-map.html
/instructor-solutions/lesson-plans.html
/instructor-solutions/homework-planner.html
/instructor-solutions/slides/*.html
/instructor-solutions/slides/*_files/
/instructor-solutions/facilitator-notes/*.html
/instructor-solutions/facilitator-notes/*_files/
# Standalone HTML reports now route directly into _site/ so the syllabus,
# slides, and facilitator-notes links across them resolve. The whole
# _site/ tree is already gitignored above via /instructor-solutions/_site/.

# Per-chapter solution YAMLs are instructor-only — keep them off the public repo.
# The public exercises/NN.yml files contain prompts/sections/webr code only;
# `R/exercise_helpers.R` falls back to "[solution withheld]" placeholders if the
# private NN-solutions.yml file is absent (e.g., a student clone).
exercises/*-solutions.yml

# Ignore Quarto's transient project state but keep the freeze cache,
# which encodes per-chapter knit results so CI can skip re-execution.
/.quarto/*
!/.quarto/_freeze/
!/.quarto/_freeze/**
# Cocoa file API auto-suffixes "<name> 2.png", "<name> 3.png", etc. when
# Quarto's render races on file creation. They're always duplicates of
# the un-suffixed original — never track them.
/.quarto/_freeze/**/* [0-9].*
**/*.quarto_ipynb

































/.luarc.json









































/.quarto/
